# DIAGNOSTICS

The Swift decoder reports the first check a message fails: `truncated`, `tooLarge`, `unsupportedVersion`, `unknownKind`, `reservedFlags`, `outOfBounds`, `badPresence`, `nonzeroPadding`, `tooManyHandles`, `missingHandle`, `unconsumed`, `invalidUTF8`, `invalidValue` or `unexpectedMessage`.
A length that is not a multiple of 8 is `truncated`.
